</style></head><body><header><small>UPPER SAVANNAH · SOURCE WORKSPACE</small><h1>Land-cover source workspace</h1><p class="intro">Original 2025 land-cover composition across the full upstream domain, reporting polygon, utility watersheds and protection areas. Explore each source scope or a selected watershed, then export the underlying cells and areas.</p></header><main>
<div class="stats"><div class="stat"><strong>30 m</strong><span>Native source grid · EPSG:5070</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>217</strong><span>Original HUC12 units</span></div><div class="stat"><strong id="domainArea"></strong><span>Full domain, hectares</span></div><div class="stat"><strong id="reportArea"></strong><span>Reporting within model, hectares</span></div></div>
<section class="workspace"><div class="scope-control"><label for="scope">Choose a geographic support</label><select id="scope"></select><label for="metric" style="margin-top:10px">Whole-watershed map measure</label><select id="metric"><option value="boundary">Watershed boundaries</option><option value="forest">Forest cover, %</option><option value="agriculture">Pasture and crops, %</option><option value="developed">Developed land, %</option><option value="wetland">Wetlands, %</option></select><p id="metricLegend" style="font-size:12px;margin:5px 0"></p><div class="map-tools"><button id="fitScope">Fit selected support</button><button id="fullDomain">Full domain</button></div></div><div class="mapbox"><svg id="map" viewBox="0 0 900 720" role="img" aria-label="Original Upper Savannah watersheds and selected geographic support"><title>Upper Savannah source supports</title><g id="map-geometry"><g id="watersheds">__HUC_PATHS__</g><path id="active-layer"/></g><text x="28" y="35" font-size="17" font-family="Arial" fill="#171717">Grid N ↑</text><line id="scale-line" x1="50" y1="682" x2="__SCALE_END__" y2="682" stroke="#171717" stroke-width="2"/><text id="scale-text" x="50" y="704" font-size="13" font-family="Arial" fill="#171717">20 km</text></svg><div class="legend"><span class="swatch"></span><span id="legend"></span><br>Thin boundaries: original HUC12 watersheds. Click a watershed for its identifier. Display geometry is generalized; downloads retain full geometry.</div><div id="selected-huc" class="status" aria-live="polite">No watershed selected.</div></div>
<div class="panel"><div class="detail"><h2 id="scopeTitle"></h2><p id="scopeBasis"></p><dl id="scopeDetail"></dl></div><div class="note"><strong>Reporting is an intersection.</strong> The original South Carolina polygon contains 95 native source cells outside the upstream model domain. The delivered <code>sc-reporting-within-model.tif</code> excludes those cells and preserves the original polygon separately.</div><div class="note"><strong>Keep utility scopes separate.</strong> Upstream memberships, designated protection buffers and intake points have different geographic meanings. Nested protection buffers overlap and must not be added together.</div><a id="maskDownload" class="button" download>Download selected mask</a><button id="reset">Reset view</button></div></section>
<section class="tables" id="coverSection"><h2 id="coverTitle">Original land-cover composition</h2><p id="coverContext"></p><div class="toolbar"><label style="font-size:13px;font-weight:400"><input type="checkbox" id="withinModel" checked style="width:auto;min-height:0"> Intersect the selected support with the model domain</label><button id="clearHuc">Whole support</button><button id="coverExport">Export displayed classes</button></div><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Original class</th><th class="num">Cells</th><th class="num">Area, ha</th><th class="num">Share, %</th><th style="min-width:150px">Proportion</th></tr></thead><tbody id="coverRows"></tbody></table></div><p style="font-size:12px">Percentages use valid land-cover cells in the displayed selection. Forest = classes 41, 42 and 43; pasture and crops = 81 and 82; developed land = 21 through 24; wetlands = 90 and 95. These descriptive categories do not establish pollutant delivery or intervention effectiveness.</p></section><section class="tables"><h2>All nine original supports</h2><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Support</th><th class="num">Grid cells</th><th class="num">Area, ha</th><th class="num">Within model, ha</th><th class="num">HUC12 units</th></tr></thead><tbody id="scopeRows"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="tables"><h2>Watershed crosswalk</h2><p>Native grid-cell counts by original HUC12. Names and state attributes come from the retained watershed source. South Carolina membership uses the actual reporting polygon, not a state-name flag.</p><div class="toolbar"><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Find a HUC12 identifier, watershed or state" aria-label="Search watersheds"><button id="downloadCrosswalk">Export filtered CSV</button></div><p id="found" class="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>HUC12</th><th>Name</th><th>States</th><th class="num">Domain cells</th><th class="num">SC-reporting cells</th></tr></thead><tbody id="hucRows"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="downloads"><h2>Editable handoff</h2><p>Open the GeoPackage in GIS software to inspect or edit full-resolution geometries. Each raster retains the exact native land-cover transform. The separately delivered EPSG:26917 model-grid masks have a different alignment. The original inputs, source compiler and manifest accompany this view. Raster, GeoPackage and table downloads are also embedded in this page for offline use.</p><a class="button" href="vectors/geographic-support.gpkg" download>Editable GeoPackage</a><a class="button" href="tables/scope-summary.csv" download>Scope summary CSV</a><a class="button" href="tables/exact-membership-landcover.csv" download>Exact overlap combinations</a><a class="button" href="tables/original-intakes-grid-crosswalk.csv" download>Original intake crosswalk</a><a class="button" href="rasters/sc-reporting-within-model.tif" download>Model-reporting mask</a><a class="button" href="originals/nlcd2025/land-cover.tif" download>Original 2025 land cover</a><a class="button" href="tables/huc12-scope-landcover.csv" download>Complete watershed classes</a><a class="button" href="SOURCE_FILES.json" download>Source file inventory</a></section>
<details><summary>Source definitions and working geometry</summary><p>The retained original source collections include 217 domain polygons, four focus polygons, 4 and 32 utility-upstream polygons, 71 public intake points and four designated protection polygons. The original PlanningBasins2023 layer supplies the reporting polygon.</p><p>Two original Pioneer protection polygons have ring self-intersections. Their originals remain unchanged. The derived working layers use explicit polygon-only <code>make_valid</code> repairs, with exact area changes recorded in <a href="tables/geometry-working-repairs.json" download>the geometry log</a>.</p><p>The retained Pioneer S37109 intake point is outside its published protection polygons. The original intake crosswalk records point and containing-cell membership independently. The source map preserves those published geometries.</p><p>These source measurements describe actual land-cover composition, not modeled nitrogen, phosphorus or sediment export. Use the separate EPSG:26917 model-grid package with scientific model outputs. The source land-cover raster uses EPSG:5070 and requires explicit nearest-neighbour preparation to a different model grid.</p><p>Pixel membership follows <a href="https://rasterio.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/rasterio.features.html">Rasterio / GDAL all_touched=False</a>. Original Esri JSON is read using the <a href="https://gdal.org/en/stable/drivers/vector/esrijson.html">GDAL ESRIJSON driver</a>. Exact vector areas and grid-cell areas are both supplied.</p></details>
<footer class="foot">Prepared from the original retained sources on 13 October 2026. Grid: 6,443 × 6,319 cells, native 30 m, NAD83 / Conus Albers. Source year: 2025. Original model-domain identity: <code>2300d9b32a513d70503222a5d2e782e032107297214036a58e8b444a312169af</code>.<p id="runtime"></p></footer></main>
