function render(){
 $('#app').innerHTML='<header><div class="toolbar"><span class="eyebrow">Ecosystem Sciences · native scenario analysis</span><div class="buttons"><button data-action="save-review">Save review</button><button data-action="open-review">Open review</button><button class="primary" data-action="save-desk">Save complete desk</button><button data-action="print">Print report</button></div></div><h1>'+esc(study.title)+'</h1><p class="scope">'+esc(study.classification)+'</p><div class="pills"><span class="pill">'+study.profiles.length+' retained parameter profiles</span><span class="pill">'+study.profiles.length*3+' completed native runs</span><span class="pill">Original '+esc(study.zone_id)+' support</span></div><p class="status" id="status" role="status">Start with the native benefit ratios. Add independently reviewed expenditure and targets to explore a decision.</p><small id="storage"></small></header>'+
 '<nav aria-label="Study sections"><a href="#margins">Decision margins</a><a href="#quotes">Cost inputs</a><a href="#targets">Targets</a><a href="#maps">Native maps</a><a href="#plans">Implementation</a><a href="#notes">Review</a><a href="#sources">Original files</a></nav>'+
 '<section class="panel" id="margins"><h2>How much extra cost can the treatment bear?</h2><p class="note">The break-even ratio compares <b>annualized treatment expenditure ÷ annualized control expenditure</b>. It is calculated separately for each pollutant from their original annual avoided exports. It is not a currency value or a price quote.</p><div class="controls profile-tags">'+study.profiles.map(p=>'<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" data-profile="'+p.id+'" '+(state.included.includes(p.id)?'checked':'')+'><span>'+esc(p.title)+'<small>'+p.id.slice(0,12)+'</small></span></label>').join('')+'</div><div id="summary" class="grid"></div><div class="row controls"><div class="compact">'+field('Explore cost ratio', 'ratio','number','min="0" step="0.05"')+'</div><p class="note">A ratio of 1 means equal assumed annualized cost. Changing this ratio does not supply a financial estimate.</p></div><p id="ratio-description" class="print-only note"></p><div id="thresholds"></div><p class="note">Each threshold uses common finite support within that exact profile and its three native runs. The support mask can change between flow profiles; no uniform-mask cross-profile confidence interval is implied. The “all listed profiles” ceiling is the minimum of their defined thresholds, not a probability statement.</p></section>'+
 '<section class="panel" id="quotes"><h2>Whole-scenario expenditure</h2><p class="note">Keep capital and recurring costs separate. A missing amount stays unentered, not zero. These quotes are assumed to apply to the same complete scenario under every listed parameter profile. Assistance payments belong in their own funding analysis, not in gross implementation expenditure.</p><div class="compact">'+field('Currency','currency','text','maxlength="3" pattern="[A-Z]{3}"')+'</div><div class="two">'+costFields('treatment','Riparian treatment')+costFields('control','Matched off-riparian control')+'</div><div id="print-costs" class="print-only"></div><div id="cost-comparison"></div><div class="buttons controls"><button data-action="quote-ratio">Use entered annualized cost ratio</button><button data-action="native-inputs">Download original Economic inputs</button></div><p class="note">Annualized expenditure = capital / annuity factor + annual operation. For positive real rate r and service horizon n, the annuity factor is (1 − (1 + r)<sup>−n</sup>) / r; at r = 0 it is n. Costs, funding, and scientific benefits are not combined into one invented monetary benefit.</p></section>'+
